# Line-ending and diff policy for Factions.
#
# Why: this repo is edited on Linux and built/deployed on Windows. Without a
# canonical policy, every cross-platform save rewrites EOLs and produces huge
# whitespace-only diffs (see AGENTS.md "Known pitfalls"). Policy:
#   - Text code/docs are stored LF in the repo, checked out native.
#   - Windows PowerShell scripts stay CRLF (PS 5.1 / Windows tooling).
#   - Vendored binaries are never touched.

# Default: let Git decide text vs binary, normalize stored EOL to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Source & docs: explicit LF (repo canonical) ---
*.cs    text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
.gitignore   text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# --- Windows scripts: keep CRLF ---
# PowerShell on the Windows deploy host (PS 5.1) is encoding/EOL sensitive.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# --- Binaries: never normalize or diff as text ---
*.dll   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.exe   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.wav   binary
*.svg   binary
*.ico   binary

# Real Gas Giants' own Config.xml bytes, kept exact: no BOM under an encoding="utf-16" declaration,
# CRLF. RggConfigWriterTests asserts XDocument.Load still refuses it, which a normalised copy need not.
tests/Factions.Core.Tests/Fixtures/rgg_config_live.xml -text
